WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.800
One of the most used pieces of notation in biochemistry began as a typographic fix.

2
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.520
Measuring hydrogen ions threw off columns of decimals, written out and re-compared

3
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:19.280
until the bookkeeping itself became the bottleneck, so a brewery chemist compressed

4
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.920
the mess into a logarithm.

5
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.180
He did not think he had discovered anything.

6
00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:28.233
Across more than a hundred and sixty pages laid out electrode by electrode,

7
00:00:28.773 --> 00:00:33.493
indicator by indicator, the choice that would outlast him appears exactly once,

8
00:00:34.013 --> 00:00:39.033
without emphasis: "For the number representing the exponent of this power, I have

9
00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.813
chosen the symbol pH."

10
00:00:41.693 --> 00:00:43.673
Two lowercase letters, buried.

11
00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:49.213
What his measurements did show, and what he did underline, was that enzymes do not

12
00:00:49.213 --> 00:00:54.573
care how much acid is present in total only about the concentration of free protons.

13
00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:59.777
He proved it on the same invertase reaction that had defeated Victor Henri, whose

14
00:00:59.777 --> 00:01:04.617
earlier results were leaky because no pH scale yet existed to fix the acidity.

15
00:01:05.297 --> 00:01:09.977
Plotted on Sørensen's new logarithmic axis, the data showed a sharp activity peak

16
00:01:09.977 --> 00:01:11.137
the old units had hidden.
